        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x - 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x - 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x - 2) + B(x + 1)$.<br>Set $x = -1$: $3(-1) + 5 = A(-3) + B(0)$, so $2 = -3A$, thus $A = -\\frac{2}{3}$.<br>Set $x = 2$: $3(2) + 5 = A(0) + B(3)$, so $11 = 3B$, thus $B = \\frac{11}{3}$.<br>The partial fractions are $\\frac{-2/3}{x + 1} + \\frac{11/3}{x - 2}$.</p>",
